        "original_id": "ce1a7e83-eefa-50da-9b4d-8b2733481cda",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: International Grenfell Association\n- People: Sir Wilfred Grenfell\n- Places: Newfoundland, Labrador, northern Newfoundland, Battle Harbour, Mary's Harbour\n- Topics: health care, education, religious services, rehabilitation, medical missions, hospital relocation, boarding school, fire\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Wilfred Thomason Grenfell was born on 28 February 1865 and died on 9 October 1940.\n- Sir Wilfred Grenfell was a medical missionary to Newfoundland and Labrador.\n- The International Grenfell Association was founded by Sir Wilfred Grenfell.\n- The International Grenfell Association provided health care, education, religious services, rehabilitation, and other social activities to fishing and coastal communities in northern Newfoundland and along the coast of Labrador.\n- After a fire destroyed its hospital and boarding school in Battle Harbour, the International Grenfell Association decided to relocate them to Mary's Harbour.",
